Third-party material bundled in this repository:

Spell-check dictionaries in public/dictionaries/ are derived from
"all-words-in-all-languages" (https://github.com/eymenefealtun/all-words-in-all-languages),
processed by scripts/build-dictionaries.mjs.

Web fonts are supplied at build time by the @fontsource packages listed in
package.json; each family carries its own upstream license (SIL Open Font
License or Apache License 2.0).

The HEIF encoder is supplied at build time by the elheif package (MIT), which
compiles libheif (LGPL-3.0), libde265 (LGPL-3.0) and kvazaar (BSD-3-Clause) to
WebAssembly. It is emitted as a file of its own (assets/heif.worker-*.js) and
can be replaced with a rebuild of those libraries. HEVC, the codec it writes,
is covered by patents; distributing an encoder for it commercially may require
a patent licence.
